            <ArticleTitle>Oxybutynin chloride in control of post-trasurethral vesical pain and spasm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>237-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oxybutynin chloride (Ditropan) and placebo were randomized in a double-blind trial to determine the effectiveness of the test agent in controlling post-transurethral pain and spasm. Oxybutynin chloride was found effective in controlling pain and spasm; no significant side effects were noted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
